  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "XXX and YYY are binary sequences of length NNN, i.e. 0≤Xi,Yi≤10 \\le X_i, Y_i \\le 10≤Xi​,Yi​≤1. There are 444 positive integer parameters AAA, BBB, CCC, and DDD.\n\nYou can do the following set of operations any number of times:\n\n\nChoose 222 indices iii and jjj such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i &lt; j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N.\nPerform **exactly** one of the following actions:\n\nSwap XiX_iXi​ and XjX_jXj​, paying a cost of AAA if Xi=1X_i = 1Xi​=1 (after the swap) and otherwise a cost of BBB.\nSwap YiY_iYi​ and YjY_jYj​, paying a cost of CCC if Yi=1Y_i = 1Yi​=1 (after the swap) and otherwise a cost of DDD.\n\n\nDefine f(X,Y)f(X, Y)f(X,Y) as the minimum cost to make the sequences XXX and YYY equal. If it is not possible to make them equal, f(X,Y)=0f(X, Y) = 0f(X,Y)=0.\n\nGiven NNN, AAA, BBB, CCC and DDD, consider the 4N4^N4N pairs of binary sequences XXX and YYY (both of length NNN). Find the sum of f(X,Y)f(X, Y)f(X,Y) over all such pairs.\n\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 555 integers - NNN, AAA, BBB, CCC and DDD.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of f(X,Y)f(X, Y)f(X,Y) over all 4N4^N4N pairs of binary sequences of length NNN modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤201 \\le T \\le 201≤T≤20",
      "1≤N≤4001 \\le N \\le 4001≤N≤400",
      "1≤A,B,C,D&lt;9982443531 \\le A, B, C, D \\lt 9982443531≤A,B,C,D&lt;998244353",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 400400400."
    ],
